  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "98c1ed74-cdd1-456a-921f-44c601cb370e",
    "name": "sandbox-svc",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "sandbox-svc — the favorite-items feature (FEAT-001) and the CSV export\n(FEAT-003).\n\nFour routes: favorite an item, list your favorites, un-favorite one, and\nexport your favorites as a CSV download. Every route acts on the calling\nuser's own rows only; the user is taken from the access token, never from\nthe request, so no route accepts a user id.\n\nPaths, methods and tags for the three JSON routes are emitted by\nnexcommon's own generator (`GenerateSwaggerDocs`, served at\n`/swagger/swagger.yaml`), so they cannot drift from the routes the service\nregisters. `GET /v1/favorites/export` is the exception: it is registered\ndirectly on the mux router, because the response is a file with its own\nheaders rather than the JSON envelope, so the generator cannot see it and\nthis document is its only contract. The response side of every route — the\n`{success, header, payload}` envelope, the per-status coverage, the\nbusiness error codes, and examples taken from the real DTOs — is authored\nhere for the same reason.\n",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
